<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/clipboard.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/clipboard-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/clipboard.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="680" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/policy-math-tools/">Free tools</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Checkup for Your Claim File</h1><p class="lede">Strong appraisals are built before the demand letter goes out. Answer twelve quick questions to see where your file stands and what to fix first.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness checkup</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation of what the insurer has accepted. If the claim was denied, talk with an Idaho attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full line-item estimate, not just the payment summary."><span>Do you have the insurer’s complete, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator. A one-line bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note the date of each. Take new photos of current conditions too."><span>Did you photograph the damage soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Look in the policy conditions for a paragraph titled ‘Appraisal’ and note any time limits it sets."><span>Have you found and read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ clause and put the date on your calendar. Our timeline builder can help."><span>Do you know the suit-limitation period in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Finish reasonable temporary repairs, like tarps or water extraction, and keep every receipt."><span>Are temporary repairs done, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure attics, wall cavities, framing and subfloors were inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request your declarations page from the insurer or agent."><span>Do you have a current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather letters, emails and claim notes in date order in one folder."><span>Is your correspondence with the insurer organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in our claim gap estimator. A small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than about 10% of the estimate, or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, return it within the time the policy allows."><span>If the insurer requested a sworn proof of loss, has it been sent on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out ready-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3ebf5" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#FFE835" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Questions about coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight. They decide whether appraisal is even the right tool and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork items matter too, but they’re easier to fix.</p>
<h2>Reading your result</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and above:</strong> your file is in good shape. A professional review of the gap is a sensible next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first. Each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now could lock in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about the appraisal readiness checkup</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is anything I enter saved?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The checkup runs entirely in your browser. Nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share the result?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot or copy your to-do list and bring it to a consultation.</p></div></details></div>
